WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.680
Making sense of the X-Men timeline can be
complicated, but when you focus just on Wolverine,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.340
the story gets a little easier to follow.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.440
From his bloody origin tale to his fateful
final movie, here’s Wolverine’s cinematic

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.440
story explained.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.540
The first chronological glimpse we get of
the boy who grows up to become Wolverine is

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:24.340
in 2009's X-Men Origins: Wolverine, where
we learn that his name isn't Logan at all.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.880
It's James Howlett.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.260
Logan is actually the surname of the man who
murders James' father in 1845, which causes

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:37.120
James' mutation to activate, pushing bone
claws out from between his knuckles.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:43.280
Enraged, James kills Logan, only to almost
immediately learn that the man was actually

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.520
his biological father.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.860
Young James flees his home along with his
half-brother, Victor Creed, who possesses

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.420
the same mutant healing ability as James.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.080
That healing factor not only makes the boys
practically impossible to kill, but also slows

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.160
their aging, keeping them looking relatively
youthful as they fight side by side through

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:04.020
every major war over the next hundred years.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:11.240
In 2013's The Wolverine, we see that he spent
some of this time in a Japanese POW camp in

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:11.900
1945.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.860
While he's there, James saves the life of
Japanese officer Ichirō Yashida from the

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.020
bombing of Nagasaki, an event which will prove
important many years later.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.820
In X-Men: First Class, Charles Xavier and
Erik Lehnsherr, soon to be known as Professor

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.880
X and Magneto, find themselves up against
Nazi mutant Sebastian Shaw and his team of

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.440
superpowered henchmen.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.140
Realizing they'll need some help to bring
Shaw down, the duo uses Cerebro to find new

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:44.060
mutants and form a team of their own, so in
a zippy montage set in 1962, they recruit

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:49.320
a handful of young mutants who wind up as
the, well, first class of X-Men.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.640
Not everyone is eager to join up, though.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:58.260
When Erik and Charles walk into a bar, a cigar-smoking
James Howlett tells them that he's not interested,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.820
using some language that insured the movie
would be a hard PG-13.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.080
While fighting together in the Vietnam War,
an increasingly violent Victor assaults a

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.500
woman, and then kills the officer who tries
to intervene.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.740
James rushes to his brother's aid without
realizing what he's done, and both are sentenced

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.320
to die by firing squad.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.780
Needless to say, the execution doesn't go
according to plan.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.500
Their miraculous survival catches the eye
of Major William Stryker, and Victor and James

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.950
are recruited to his black ops team of mutants,
Team X, which also includes a version of Wade

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:35.500
Wilson, better known as Deadpool, that we
all do our best to just not talk about.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.260
"Hey!

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.180
It's me!

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.520
Don't scratch!"

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:44.020
It's at this point that James starts going
by the alias Logan, after the father he killed

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:44.920
so many decades before.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.400
Logan and Victor work with Team X for several
years, but ultimately, Logan decides he can

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.000
no longer stomach the team's callous disdain
for human life.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.940
He quits Team X, but Victor decides to stay,
and the two part ways.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:04.160
Six years after walking away from Team X,
Logan is working as a lumberjack in the Canadian

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.540
Rockies, but is pulled back into Stryker's
world after Victor murders Logan's girlfriend,

00:03:08.549 --> 00:03:09.700
Kayla Silverfox.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:15.360
Stryker tells him Victor has gone rogue, and
he asks Logan to join the Weapon X program,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:20.069
giving him a chance to get his revenge on
Victor by undergoing an experimental procedure

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:23.800
that will fuse an unbreakable metal called
adamantium to his skeleton.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:29.460
Wolverine agrees, after requesting new dog
tags with the alias "Wolverine."

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.360
Thanks to the healing factor that allows him
to survive, the procedure is a success.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:39.020
Stryker, never intended to let Logan go free
once it was completed, but Logan manages to

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:39.520
escape.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.160
When he learns that Victor is kidnapping young
mutants for Stryker, Logan returns to free

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.200
them and get his revenge.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.980
The young mutants are flown to safety by Charles
Xavier while Logan and Victor fight, first

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:54.060
against each other, then together against
Deadpool.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.920
Once Wade is defeated, Victor leaves, but
before Logan can get out, Stryker shoots him

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.240
in the head with an adamantium bullet.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.900
Logan survives, but when he regains consciousness,
he can't remember his past.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.600
Set in the year 2003, X-Men reveals Logan
living as a cage fighter in Canada, still

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.220
missing most of his memories but using the
alias "Wolverine" thanks to the dog tags he

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.080
got from Weapon X.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.830
He meets young mutant runaway Rogue, and they're
attacked on the road by Victor, who's now

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:22.900
called Sabretooth.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.820
Curiously, neither brother seems to have any
memory of the other, and unlike Wolverine,

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.620
Sabretooth looks like a completely different
person now.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:36.040
While Sabretooth has the upper hand, Wolverine
and Rogue are rescued by Storm and Cyclops

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.480
and taken to Charles Xavier's mansion, where
they join the X-Men.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.400
Together with the X-Men, Wolverine fights
Magneto and his Brotherhood of Mutants.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.160
The bad guys want to use Rogue's abilities
to power a device that will turn baseline

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.380
humans into mutants, in response to a proposed
law that would require mutants to register

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.580
with the government.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:59.100
The X-Men manage to foil Magneto's plot, overcoming
both the Brotherhood and some pretty rough

00:04:59.140 --> 00:04:59.640
dialogue.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.640
"Do you know what happens to a toad when it's
struck by lightning?...The same thing that

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.340
happens to everything else."

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:11.500
The X-Men's victory leads to Magneto's imprisonment,
but the tension between mutants and humans

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.000
remains.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.780
Occuring not long after the events of X-Men,
X2: X-Men United opens with a mutant assassination

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.700
attempt on the president of the United States,
causing relations between mutants and the

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.880
U.S. government to become rockier than ever.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.920
William Stryker, now much older than the last
time we saw him, receives permission from

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:35.100
the president to investigate Xavier, but it's
really a ruse so that Stryker can force Xavier

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:37.600
to use Cerebro to destroy all mutants.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:43.140
The X-Men travel to Stryker's base underneath
an abandoned military installation, and when

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.580
Logan enters the room where he received his
adamantium skeleton, some of his memories

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.080
return.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.820
He attacks Stryker, demanding to know why
the military man did this to him, and he's

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.420
shocked when Stryker reveals that Logan volunteered
for the Weapon X program.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:01.960
Logan refrains from killing his old foe, but
Stryker ultimately meets his end when a nearby

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:02.880
dam bursts, drowning him.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.320
Meanwhile, the X-Men have managed to overcome
both Stryker's people and Magneto, who tried

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:08.880
to double cross them.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:14.320
In the process, their plane is damaged, leading
Jean Grey, with whom Logan has fallen in love,

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.910
to telekinetically lift the plane to safety
while holding back the lake.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.320
Once her team is safe, she gets swept away
by the rushing water.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.620
At the beginning of X-Men: The Last Stand,
set in 2006, Cyclops goes to visit what he

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.820
thinks is Jean's final resting place.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.500
But she's not dead.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.580
Naturally, he's overjoyed to learn that she's
still alive, but his delight is short-lived

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.840
when Jean unceremoniously kills him.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:43.780
Xavier sends Logan and Storm to investigate,
and they're horrified to learn that Jean has

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.820
been taken over by a destructive power called
the Phoenix.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:52.140
Meanwhile, a so-called "cure" for mutants
has been discovered, and Magneto rebuilds

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.420
his Brotherhood of Mutants to oppose it.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.620
Feeling betrayed by Xavier, who suppressed
the Phoenix when she was a child, Jean kills

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.860
her mentor and joins with Magneto, but don't
worry.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.020
Xavier is only mostly dead.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:08.480
Magneto and the Brotherhood attack the lab
where the cure is held, but during the battle,

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:12.640
Jean loses control of the Phoenix and begins
indiscriminately destroying everything around

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:13.140
her.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.900
Thanks to his healing ability, Logan is the
only one who's able to get close to Jean.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:23.600
In a moment of lucidity, she asks Logan to
save her, and he claws into her chest, killing

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.180
her and ending the destruction.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.780
"I love you."

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:35.140
Set in 2013, The Wolverine finds Logan back
in the Canadian wilderness, still agonizing

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:40.520
over killing Jean, when he's contacted on
behalf of Ichirō Yashida, the man he saved

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.140
back in 1945.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:47.400
The message is delivered by Yukio, a mutant
who has the ability to foresee people's deaths,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.720
and who has had a vision about Wolverine.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.400
"I see you on your back.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.040
There's blood everywhere.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.880
You're holding your own heart in your hand."

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:06.540
While in Japan, Logan realizes that Yashida
didn't ask him there to say farewell.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:10.260
Instead, he wants to steal Logan's immortality
and live forever.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.500
Logan loses his adamantium claws battling
Yashida, but he manages to defeat him using

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.120
his regenerated bone claws.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:21.140
After the fight, Logan leaves Japan, accompanied
by Yukio.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.400
In a mid-credits scene set two years later,
Magneto and a very-much-alive Charles Xavier

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:30.560
approach Logan in an airport to tell him of
a new threat to wipe out all mutants.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:37.660
X-Men: Days of Future Past opens in the year
2023, when mutants have been driven to near-extinction

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.940
by the robotic Sentinels.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:45.480
Along with Xavier, Storm, and Magneto, Logan;
who miraculously has his adamantium claws

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:49.080
back; has managed to elude the Sentinels long
enough to form a plan.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.920
With the future already beyond repair, they
decide to use Kitty Pryde's mutant ability

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.980
to send Logan's consciousness back to 1973
to stop the events that led to the creation

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:02.380
of the Sentinels in the first place, kind
of like in the first Terminator.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.960
They hope that, if he's successful, the timeline
will reset, placing them all in an alternate

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.980
version of 2023.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:16.720
Using his 1973 body piloted by his 2023 consciousness,
Logan joins forces with the younger Xavier

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:21.300
and his X-Men to prevent the assassination
that paves the way for the Sentinel program.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.980
Although Logan succeeds in his mission, he's
horribly injured in the process, with his

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:29.060
mangled body sinking to the bottom of the
Potomac River.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.820
However, Logan's 2023 consciousness doesn't
stick around long enough to learn how he survives.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:39.140
As soon as he changes the future, he returns
to an alternate 2023.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.780
In this new timeline, Logan is now a teacher
in Xavier's school, where many of the X-Men

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.660
who'd died in the primary timeline are now
alive again, including Jean Grey.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:54.180
After completing his mission in Days of Future
Past, Logan's maimed body is recovered by

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:58.920
a team led by a person who appears to be Stryker,
but is revealed to be Mystique.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.900
In X-Men: Apocalypse, it seems that Logan
somehow wound up back under the real Stryker's

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:04.820
control anyway.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:10.840
In yet another new timeline, he never escaped
the Weapon X program after gaining his adamantium

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.700
skeleton in 1979.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.380
The X-Men come upon this alternate version
of Logan, who's still being called Weapon

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:21.720
X and has no memory of his true identity,
when they infiltrate Stryker's facility in

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.100
1983.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.180
After Wolverine slaughters many of Stryker's
soldiers, Jean Grey manages to restore some

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.100
of his memories.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:34.480
Logan runs out into the cold, and Cyclops
speculates that they'll never see him again.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.780
Presumably, Jean's intervention paves the
way for Logan to still join the X-Men at some

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:42.840
point down the road, leading to the happy
timeline we saw in Days of Future Past.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:44.440
Or maybe not.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:49.380
The Wolverine we meet in Logan is a much older,
more beaten-down version of the character

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.300
than moviegoers had seen before.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:57.160
After living for nearly two centuries, Logan's
healing ability is finally beginning to fail,

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.140
and he's growing increasingly ill from adamantium
poisoning.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:05.400
This future version of Logan is working as
a limo driver and caring for an ailing Charles

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.100
Xavier, and he carries around an adamantium
bullet, pondering the possibility of ending

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.000
his own life.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:16.020
Despite the happy future Logan returned to
at the end of Days of Future Past, we learn

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.580
that most mutants, including the X-Men, have
been wiped out anyway.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.520
It wasn't the government this time, though:
A few years before the start of the film,

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.310
Xavier lost control of his powers and inadvertently
killed the rest of the X-Men, a fact which

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:32.480
Logan remembers, but Charles has mercifully
forgotten.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:39.540
"I did something…something unspeakable."

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:46.140
In 2029, Logan encounters a young girl named
Laura whose powers mirror his own.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:51.180
This kid is determined to get to a mutant
sanctuary in North Dakota called Eden.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:55.280
Charles persuades Logan to take her there,
and the three embark on the journey together.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:12:00.460
Along the way, they learn that Laura was created
using Logan's DNA as part of the villainous

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:01.540
Transigen program.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:08.720
Unfortunately, that DNA was also used to create
X24, a vicious clone that looks exactly like

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.020
Logan did in his prime.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:16.120
Before they can reach Eden, X24 kills Charles,
but Logan and Laura manage to escape.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:19.340
Laura convinces Logan to continue onto Eden,
and when they get there, they find the other

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:22.500
mutant children who've escaped Transigen.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.320
Laura and the kids make plans to escape into
Canada, but before they can, they're attacked

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:29.960
by Transigen soldiers and X24.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.060
The children defeat the soldiers, but Logan
is no match for his new and improved clone,

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.600
who impales him on a fallen tree.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:42.020
Before X24 can finish him off, Laura shoots
him in the head with Logan's adamantium bullet.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:45.180
Logan dies holding Laura's hand, metaphorically
fulfilling Yukio's vision that he would die

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.540
with "his heart in his hand."

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:53.360
Laura and the other mutant children escape
to Canada, leaving behind Wolverine's grave,

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:54.620
which is marked with an "X."

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.780
